   "html_text": "Curry’s correspondence between propositions and types was extended to predicate logic in the late 1960s by Howard (1980) and de Bruijn (1970). At around the same time Lawvere developed related ideas in categorical logic. In particular he proposed the notion of a hyperdoctrine (Lawvere 1970) as a categorical model of (typed) predicate logic. A hyperdoctrine is an indexed category ⟦M⟧ , where ⟦M⟧ is a category with objects representing types and arrows representing terms. If ⟦M⟧ is a type then ⟦M⟧",
